---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { t, type Lang } from '../lib/i18n';
interface Props { lang: Lang }
const { lang } = Astro.props;
const en = lang === 'en';
---
<Base lang={lang} title={t(lang, 'method.title') + ' · Sinan Robo'} active="methodology" path="/methodology" crumbs={[{ label: t(lang, 'nav.methodology') }]}>
  <div class="rise" style="--i:0;margin-bottom:14px"><h1 style="font-size:24px">{t(lang, 'method.title')}</h1></div>
  <section class="card pad prose rise" style="--i:1">
  {en ? <>
    <h2>1. What we measure</h2>
    <p>One measurement unit is <code>model version × hardware × precision (fp16 / int8 …) × batch = 1 × input resolution × action-chunk length</code>. Metrics: single-step inference latency p50 / p95 (ms), first-action latency, throughput (action chunks per second), peak VRAM (GB), power (optional).</p>
    <h2>2. How a run is done</h2>
    <ol><li>Warm up for at least 20 steps before timing; then time at least 200 steps.</li><li>Fix input resolution and action-chunk length; record both in <code>config</code>.</li><li>Record a hardware fingerprint: GPU model, driver, CUDA, CPU, RAM, OS, power mode.</li><li>Report p50 and p95. Never report a single run as “the” latency.</li></ol>
    <h2>3. Sources and their labels</h2>
    <p>Every number carries one of three source types, always shown next to it: <span class="pill literature">Literature</span> (from a paper or official doc), <span class="pill maintainer">Maintainer measured</span> (run by Sinan Lab), <span class="pill crowd">Crowd upload</span> (from the CLI). A configuration becomes “verified” only after at least three independent contributors or a maintainer re-run agree.</p>
    <h2>4. Display rules</h2>
    <ul><li>Fewer than 3 samples: shown with a <span class="pill pending">Preliminary (n&lt;3)</span> badge.</li><li>Values more than 3σ from the median are quarantined for review and not displayed.</li><li>Unverified fields are shown as <span class="pill pending">Unverified</span>. We never fill them with defaults.</li></ul>
    <h2>5. Cost</h2>
    <p><code>cost per 1k inferences (CNY) = p50 ms ÷ 1000 × hourly rental (CNY) ÷ 3600 × 1000</code>. The rental price is the card's public on-demand hourly rate from the Sinan Compute price library, with source and date shown. If either input is missing, the cell shows “—” and the reason.</p>
    <h2>6. What we do not say</h2>
    <p>We state measurements and conditions. We do not rank models as better or worse; fitness depends on the task, and that judgment is yours.</p>
    <h2>7. Crowd CLI (planned)</h2>
    <pre>sinan-bench hw                          # hardware fingerprint
sinan-bench run --model gr00t-n1.7 --steps 200 --precision fp16
sinan-bench report --last              # local JSON / Markdown report
sinan-bench upload --last              # metrics + fingerprint only; no images, data or keys</pre>
    <p>Uploads carry only metrics and the hardware fingerprint. Same fingerprint and configuration are de-duplicated within 24 hours.</p>
    <h2 id="world">8. World models: what we record and how</h2>
    <p><b>Scope.</b> Models the publisher calls a world model that predict later frames or states from the current view plus a condition (robot action, camera path, keyboard / mouse, or text). Downloadable weights, API-only, demo-only and announced-only systems are all listed, with the access type shown.</p>
    <ul><li><b>Available since</b> is the day weights or the API actually became available, not the paper date.</li><li><b>Parameters</b> come from the model card or weight metadata; when they differ from the marketing number we use the metadata and say so.</li><li><b>Licences</b> are copied verbatim, code and weights separately. “Commercial OK” is set only when both allow it; conflicts between README, model card and mirror leave it unverified.</li><li><b>Speed, resolution, length and VRAM</b> are the publisher’s own statements and are labelled “claimed”. They are not our measurements.</li></ul>
    <p><b>Our measurements (in preparation).</b> (1) Speed and VRAM: the official inference script on RTX 4090 / RTX 5090 / A800 at a fixed resolution and frame count; frames generated per second and peak VRAM, with the hardware fingerprint. (2) A physics test set: a fixed set of short prompts run every month on every accessible model (an object falls, something hidden reappears, a cup is pushed off a table, water is poured, the camera circles a product, a walk through a shop). Clips are published side by side and each item is marked pass / fail / can’t tell by written rules. No overall score and no ranking.</p>
  </> : <>
    <h2>1. 测什么</h2>
    <p>一个测量单元是 <code>模型版本 × 硬件 × 精度（fp16 / int8 …）× 批大小 = 1 × 输入分辨率 × 动作块长度</code>。指标：单步推理延迟 p50 / p95（毫秒）、首动作延迟、吞吐（每秒动作块数）、显存峰值（GB）、功耗（可选）。</p>
    <h2>2. 怎么跑</h2>
    <ol><li>先预热至少 20 步再计时；计时至少 200 步。</li><li>固定输入分辨率与动作块长度，两者都写进 <code>config</code>。</li><li>记录硬件指纹：GPU 型号、驱动、CUDA、CPU、内存、操作系统、电源模式。</li><li>报告 p50 和 p95。单次结果不能当“延迟”。</li></ol>
    <h2>3. 来源与标签</h2>
    <p>每个数字旁边永远带三种来源标签之一：<span class="pill literature">文献值</span>（论文或官方文档）、<span class="pill maintainer">维护者实测</span>（司南实验室跑的）、<span class="pill crowd">众包上传</span>（CLI 上传）。同一配置至少 3 个独立贡献者或维护者复测一致，才标“已验证”。</p>
    <h2>4. 展示规则</h2>
    <ul><li>样本少于 3 条：带 <span class="pill pending">初步（样本&lt;3）</span> 徽标。</li><li>偏离中位数超过 3σ 的值隔离待审，不展示。</li><li>没核实的字段显示 <span class="pill pending">待核实</span>，绝不用默认值填。</li></ul>
    <h2>5. 成本口径</h2>
    <p><code>每千次推理成本（元）= 延迟 p50 ÷ 1000 × 小时租价（元）÷ 3600 × 1000</code>。租价取该卡在 Sinan Compute 价格库里的公开按需小时价，来源和日期一并显示。任一输入缺失，格子显示“—”并写明原因。</p>
    <h2>6. 我们不说什么</h2>
    <p>我们只陈述测量值和条件，不给模型排优劣。合不合用取决于你的任务，判断权在你。</p>
    <h2>7. 众包 CLI（规划中）</h2>
    <pre>sinan-bench hw                          # 采集硬件指纹
sinan-bench run --model gr00t-n1.7 --steps 200 --precision fp16
sinan-bench report --last              # 本地 JSON / Markdown 报告
sinan-bench upload --last              # 只传指标和硬件指纹，不传图像、数据、密钥</pre>
    <p>上传只含指标与硬件指纹。同一指纹、同一配置 24 小时内去重。</p>
    <h2 id="world">8. 世界模型：收什么、怎么记</h2>
    <p><b>收录范围。</b>发布方称为世界模型、能根据当前画面加一个条件（机器人动作、镜头轨迹、键鼠或文字）预测之后画面或状态的模型。可下载权重、只有接口、只有体验入口、只宣布的都收，并标明获取方式。</p>
    <ul><li><b>可用日期</b>取权重或接口真正能用的那天，不是论文日期。</li><li><b>参数量</b>取模型卡或权重元数据；和宣传数字不一致时用元数据，并写明。</li><li><b>许可证</b>照抄原文，代码和权重分开记。两个都明确允许才记“可商用”；README、模型卡、镜像说法冲突的记“待核实”。</li><li><b>速度、分辨率、时长、显存</b>都是发布方自己的说法，标“官方声称”，不是我们测的。</li></ul>
    <p><b>我们的实测（准备中）。</b>① 速度与显存：用官方推理脚本，在 RTX 4090 / RTX 5090 / A800 上固定分辨率和帧数，测每秒生成帧数和显存峰值，附硬件指纹。② 物理考题：一套固定的短题，每月对所有能用的模型同题生成（东西掉下来、挡住后再出现、杯子被推下桌、倒水、镜头绕产品一圈、在店里走一遍等）。视频并排公开，按写好的规则逐题记“过 / 不过 / 看不出”，不算综合分，不排名。</p>
  </>}
  </section>
</Base>
